WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.879
Idea. Partners make a profit together. But who gets what? They follow their partnership agreement: first some extras for each partner, then the rest is split in an agreed ratio. The appropriation account shows exactly how the profit is shared.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:29.651
Start with profit for the year. Add interest on drawings, because partners pay it. Take off interest on capital and salaries. What is left, the residual profit, is shared in the profit-sharing ratio.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:46.027
Method. Work out each partner's figures. Interest on drawings is a percentage of total drawings, including goods taken. Interest on capital is a percentage of each capital. A monthly salary is multiplied by twelve.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:58.397
Share the residual profit in the ratio, and check the shares add back to it. Interest on a partner's loan is not in this account: it is an expense, taken off before profit for the year.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:12.959
Worked example. Here is a real question from June 2023. Prepare Belen and Charo's appropriation account for the year ended thirty-first December 2022. Eight marks.

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:25.603
They share profits equally. Interest on capital is five per cent of opening capital, interest on drawings is eight per cent of total drawings, and Charo gets two thousand dollars a month.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:37.313
Profit for the year was sixty-six thousand two hundred. Now look at the drawings. Charo also took goods worth two thousand for her own use. Goods taken count as drawings too.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:53.589
Belen drew twenty thousand. Charo drew thirty-six thousand in cash, plus two thousand in goods: thirty-eight thousand. At eight per cent, that is one thousand six hundred and three thousand and forty: four thousand six hundred and forty to add.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:02:07.002
Interest on capital: five per cent of eighty thousand is four thousand, and of ninety thousand is four thousand five hundred. Charo's salary is two thousand times twelve: twenty-four thousand.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:24.888
Residual profit: sixty-six thousand two hundred, plus four thousand six hundred and forty, minus eight thousand five hundred, minus twenty-four thousand, is thirty-eight thousand three hundred and forty. Shared equally, that is nineteen thousand one hundred and seventy each.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:40.660
Here is the finished account. Interest on drawings is added, interest on capital and the salary are taken off, and the shares add back to the residual. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:49.511
Common mistake. A common mistake is taking interest on drawings off. Partners pay it to the business, so it is added.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:55.613
Another is using the monthly salary as the yearly figure. Multiply by twelve.

00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:06.976
Your turn. Now you try. Ana and Ben share profits three to two. Read their agreement, then prepare the appropriation account. Pause here and work it out.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:22.898
Answer. Interest on drawings is five hundred and four hundred: nine hundred to add. Interest on capital is five thousand and three thousand. Ben's salary is twelve thousand. The residual is forty thousand nine hundred.

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:34.809
Ana gets three fifths: twenty-four thousand five hundred and forty. Ben gets two fifths: sixteen thousand three hundred and sixty. Together that is forty thousand nine hundred.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:46.244
Remember: start with profit, add interest on drawings, take off interest on capital and salaries, then share the rest and check. Now try the practice questions.
